Hi,

The issue is that certain peptides that are shared across multiple possible proteins.  For example, for peptide "A.Q(-17.03)DSTSDLIPAPPLSK.V", the following proteins were quantified for run 2: NGAL_HUMAN, B2ZDQ1, and X6R8F3.

What upstream processing tool do you use for identification / quantification? E.g. MaxQuant, DIANN, Fragpipe, etc.  MSstats has converters as part of the MSstatsConvert <https://www.bioconductor.org/packages/release/bioc/html/MSstatsConvert.html> package that can convert your quantification report into MSstats format.  These converters filter out any peptides that are shared across multiple proteins.

Thanks,
Tony

